{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "The harness's own record of which licence governs the model weights that ComfyUI workflow templates download, keyed by Hugging Face repo id. A repo that is not listed is unknown. The catalog reads it to class a template and to decide whether running it needs an acknowledgement; it never grants anything.",
  "default_class": "unknown",
  "classes": {
    "permissive": "The repo declares a licence that allows commercial use without further conditions.",
    "conditional": "Commercial use depends on conditions: revenue or user thresholds, excluded territories, notices, terms nobody has read, or a base model's licence. Needs an explicit acknowledgement.",
    "non_commercial": "The repo declares a non-commercial licence. Needs an explicit acknowledgement that names it.",
    "unknown": "No entry, or the repo declares no licence. Handled like conditional until somebody reads the licence."
  },
  "evidence": "Repo-level licence tags from the Hugging Face model API (cardData and tags), as digested on 2026-09-30 during a research pass; none of these entries was re-fetched when the map was written. An entry whose basis begins `inferred from` was copied from the sibling repo it names, not read, and carries no source_url or fetched_on. A tag is not a per-file licence: a repo can host files under another licence, and one repo (a shared encoder host) is tagged for a different model family than some of its files. Conditions text comes from digests of licence texts and was not read in full. Treat every conditional or non_commercial entry as a pointer to the licence, not a summary of it.",
  "flux_bar": "flux_bar true marks a repo the FLUX-family bar (ADR 0011) applies to; false exempts a repo the name pattern would otherwise catch. Without the field, the catalog's name pattern decides. These entries exist so the gate can refuse those templates; they are not recommendations.",
